# g96-be-shared: what the wiring applies (no Cargo edge, no protocol row, nothing to remove from SERVICE_PENDING)

1. compose_flip.rs `real_core`, right after `room_sessions` is built (the `DirectorySessions::new(directory.clone(), threads.clone())
   .with_archive_stamps(..).with_routes(..)` value), once the session directory can open threads:

       if let Err(error) = room_sessions.import_node_hidden(b.data_dir.clone(), b.tokens.interactive_io).await {
           tracing::warn!("[session-hidden] the Node daemon's hidden set was not imported: {error:?}");
       }

   It reads `<data>/session-hidden.json` once, stamps `archivedAt` on the sessions it names that still exist and are
   not archived, and records the import in `<data>/session-hidden.imported` (the file itself is kept).

2. compose_flip.rs `real_core`, AFTER `agent_evidence.bind(Arc::new(..SessionAgentEvidence::new(..)))` (the stamp reads the
   home threads' greeting through that evidence; unbound it reads no greeting and would stamp a greeted bot `kind: agent`),
   and before the first catalog read that serves a client (Node ran `migrateAgentKindMarkers` then `migrateBotStore` at the
   agent editor's first use). `agents` is the `Arc<AgentDefinitions>` that `build_agents(..)` returned:

       {
           let guard = mixdog_core_config::user_data::UserData::process();
           let data = b.data_dir.clone();
           if let Err(error) = agents
               .migrate_agent_store(Arc::new(move |lane, reason| {
                   if let Err(error) = guard.backup_user_data(lane, &data, reason, &mixdog_core_config::user_data::BOT_SPLIT_BACKUP_DIRS) {
                       tracing::warn!("[user-data-backup] {reason}: {error:?}");
                   }
               }))
               .await
           {
               tracing::warn!("[bot-split] the agent store migrations did not run: {error}");
           }
       }

   Each step reports its own failure and retries at the next start (Ok((KindReport, SplitReport))).
   `backup_user_data` takes a WriteLane: the closure receives the DurabilityIo lane of the job.

3. Not a hot-file edit, left open (see the review): `SessionHandle::captured_cwd()` / `UserCwd::captured_cwd()` is
   `captureOriginalUserCwd()` and has no caller yet. The prompt's env cwd of a session whose header has no cwd
   (prompt_rebuild.rs, `cwd: Some(self.cwd.as_str()).filter(..)`) still answers None where Node answered this cwd.
